SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Wed. Dec. 9 · Call 6:00 PM · 7:00 PM–7:45 PM · Robinson 
 Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 6:00 PM: dancers must b
 e checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 5:45 PM. BA: Call Time
  is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minute
 s before Call Time.\nACT I Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair an
 d Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHANG
 E — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal ar
 e the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1x
 WFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP f
 or Mice: Mice — Costume (you provide): Pink/Flesh Seamless Tights Blac
 k Camisole Leotard Male Mice: white ballet shirt\, black shorts\, pink t
 ights\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup Men's Ligh
 t Stage Makeup\; Hair: Male: Hair out of the eyes Female: High Bun\, No 
 Part\; Accessories (BA provides): Gray Gloves\nLight Stage Makeup Instru
 ction Sheet:\n•  Powder matching skintone\n•  Light brown eye 
 shadow applied to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n•  Dark Brow
 n/Black eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n•  Blush on th
 e cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in
  the stage lights)\n•  Red or Dark Red lipstick\nMen's Stage Makeup
 :\n•  Dark Brown/Black eyeliner - apply from corner to corner\n• 
  Brown or tan under cheek bone to create shadow and accentuate the ja
 w line\n•  Brown eye liner around lips and nude/flesh colored lipst
 ick\n• *Men will not look like they are wearing makeup. It will help t
 he face be seen from the stage.\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone ti
 ghts and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Han
 dle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delicat
 e fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costu
 me damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n• 
  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by 
 their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor while in
  costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder an
 y costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while in costu
 me and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume
  during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfume or co
 logne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment not assigned to c
 ast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in c
 ostume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not remove costumes fro
 m their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n•  Remove all 
 bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n• 
  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply fully w
 ith any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• 
  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may dama
 ge or stain costumes.
