SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A School Show @ 10:30 AM – ACT I Cast A (Party
  Scene\, Battle Scene\, Snow Scene) (Mandatory – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Thu. Dec. 10 · Call 9:30 AM · 10:30 AM–11:00 AM · Robins
 on Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 9:30 AM: dancers mus
 t be checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 9:15 AM. BA: Call T
 ime is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 min
 utes before Call Time.\nACT I Student Matinee Performance (to recorded s
 ound)\; NO COFFEE\, BON BON\, ANGELS.\nAll Casts are called unless a cas
 t is named. SUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA
  emails and the BA portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.
 google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\
 n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP for Mice: Mice — Costume (you provide): Pin
 k/Flesh Seamless Tights Black Camisole Leotard Male Mice: white ballet s
 hirt\, black shorts\, pink tights\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: L
 ight Stage Makeup Men's Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: Male: Hair out of the
  eyes Female: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): Gray Glove
 s\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n•  Powder matching skinto
 ne\n•  Light brown eye shadow applied to the crease with an eye sha
 dow brush\n•  Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black mascara. No fake 
 lashes.\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer 
 doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n•  Red or Dark Red 
 lipstick\nMen's Stage Makeup:\n•  Dark Brown/Black eyeliner - apply
  from corner to corner\n•  Brown or tan under cheek bone to create 
 shadow and accentuate the jaw line\n•  Brown eye liner around lips 
 and nude/flesh colored lipstick\n• *Men will not look like they are we
 aring makeup. It will help the face be seen from the stage.\nDancers of 
 Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume C
 are Guidelines:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care while changing 
 to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Ar
 kansas in the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no mat
 ter how significant\n•  Never throw costumes or accessories on the 
 floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from s
 itting on the floor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, 
 mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply 
 stage make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from
  smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n•  Refrain from th
 e use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear a
 ny garment not assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume
  food or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n• 
  Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from th
 e theater\n•  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and 
 wigs following their use\n•  Return all headpieces to their assigne
 d bags\n•  Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas
 ’ wardrobe policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored dr
 inks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
